   "clause_text": "python -m treesum build DIR -o FILE writes the same text to FILE instead — creating it, or replacing its previous content — with nothing on standard output, and exits 0. When FILE lies inside DIR, FILE is not an entry of the snapshot.",
   "requirement": "R-5.3",
   "section": "§5",
   "subject": "treesum:__main__ build -o"
  },
  "C-CLI-USAGE": {
   "clause": "5.5",
   "clause_text": "Any other use exits 2 with a message on standard error and nothing on standard output: an unknown or missing subcommand, missing or extra arguments, a DIR that is not a directory, a FILE that cannot be read or that does not parse (3.2).",
   "requirement": "R-5.5",
   "section": "§5",
   "subject": "treesum:__main__"
  },
